{"id":"pelethites","name":"Pelethites","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:pelethites"],"types":[{"type":"group","from":"UBS: Names of Groups"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Pelethites","text":"Mentioned always along with the Cherethites, and only in the time of David. The word probably means “runners” or “couriers,” and may denote that while forming part of David’s bodyguard, they were also sometimes employed as couriers (2 Sam. 8:18; 20:7, 23;1 Kings 1:38, 44; 1 Chr. 18:17). Some, however, think that these are the names simply of two Philistine tribes from which David selected his body-guard. They are mentioned along with the Gittites (2 Sam. 15:18), another body of foreign troops whom David gathered round him."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6432","lemma":"פְּלֵתִי","xlit":"Pᵉlêthîy","gloss":"a courier or official messenger","kjv":"Pelethites","count":6,"share":1},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":5,"share":0.83},{"strong":"H4428","lemma":"מֶלֶךְ","xlit":"melek","gloss":"a king","kjv":"king, royal","count":3,"share":0.5}],"verses":["2Sam.8.18","2Sam.15.18","2Sam.20.7","2Sam.20.23","1Kgs.1.38","1Chr.18.17"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"cherethites","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.545,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"abdon","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"accursed","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"achbor","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"adaiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"adrammelech","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"aharah","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121",